WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.080
DNA is written in just 4
letters: A, T, C and G.

2
00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:09.680
Proteins are built from
20 different amino acids.

3
00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:12.770
Yet a gene, a sequence of those 4 letters,

4
00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:16.790
sets the exact order of
amino acids in a polypeptide.

5
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:20.990
So how can 4 letters spell out
20 different building blocks?

6
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:25.760
In this mission, you'll count how many
different words 4 letters can make.

7
00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:29.160
Then you'll take a real
stretch of RNA and decode it,

8
00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:32.650
step by step, into a chain of amino acids.

9
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:37.960
Your mission: find out how a gene's 4
letters spell out a protein built from 20

10
00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.390
different building blocks.
